<!-- What the TV itself shows, in both of its likely languages. Before the phone connects it can't know the TV's
     language, so screens that send the user into the TV's menus show both (Ui.tvText). Not translated: each
     pair is already both languages. Wording follows Android TV / Google TV; some brands word it a little
     differently. Arabic paths use "›" like English: it is a mirrored character, so right-to-left text draws it
     pointing left, the way Arabic reads. Typing "‹" there would draw it pointing right. -->
